<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">Best Public Domain & Creative Commons Video Sources</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Finding high-quality video that you can legally download and reuse is simple when you know where to look. Public domain and Creative Commons (CC) content can be used in personal projects, education, presentations, and even commercial work depending on the license.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">What is public domain?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Public domain videos are not protected by copyright. This usually happens when copyright expires, the creator explicitly waives rights, or the work was created by a U.S. federal agency. You can download, edit, and share these videos freely.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">What is Creative Commons?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Creative Commons licenses let creators share their work with clear permissions. Common licenses include:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li><strong>CC0:</strong> No rights reserved — use for any purpose.</li>
        <li><strong>CC BY:</strong> Use with attribution to the creator.</li>
        <li><strong>CC BY-SA:</strong> Share and remix, but share-alike under the same license.</li>
        <li><strong>CC BY-NC:</strong> Non-commercial use only.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Top public domain video sources</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li><strong>Internet Archive:</strong> A massive library of films, TV, newsreels, and old commercials.</li>
        <li><strong>NASA:</strong> Space footage, mission videos, and educational clips.</li>
        <li><strong>Pexels and Pixabay:</strong> Modern stock videos shared under permissive licenses.</li>
        <li><strong>Library of Congress:</strong> Historical American films and recordings.</li>
        <li><strong>Wikimedia Commons:</strong> A wide collection of freely usable media.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">How to download these videos</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Once you find a public video, paste the URL into <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a>, select your format, and download. Always double-check the license page to confirm reuse rights.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Use responsibly</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Even free videos may require attribution or have usage limits. Read the license terms carefully and respect the creator's wishes. For more details, read our <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline">Disclaimer</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
